1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,460
What if an entire town just disappeared?

2
00:00:03,100 --> 00:00:06,940
In 1590, governor John White returned to

3
00:00:06,950 --> 00:00:09,320
Roanoke Island after years away.

4
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:11,920
He came looking for his family and

5
00:00:11,930 --> 00:00:14,320
the colonists he had left behind.

6
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:17,640
Instead, he found empty houses,

7
00:00:18,260 --> 00:00:20,580
silent paths, and no one waiting for

8
00:00:20,590 --> 00:00:20,864
him.

9
00:00:21,620 --> 00:00:23,840
Then he found one word carved into

10
00:00:23,850 --> 00:00:25,520
the settlement: Croatoan.

11
00:00:25,530 --> 00:00:27,880
It was the first sign that the

12
00:00:27,890 --> 00:00:29,680
settlers may have left alive.

13
00:00:30,160 --> 00:00:32,460
But it was only a clue and

14
00:00:32,470 --> 00:00:34,060
the people who could explain it were

15
00:00:34,070 --> 00:00:34,497
gone.

16
00:00:35,520 --> 00:00:37,580
White had been trapped across the Atlantic

17
00:00:37,590 --> 00:00:40,000
by war and failing supplies.

18
00:00:40,620 --> 00:00:41,820
Year after year,

19
00:00:42,180 --> 00:00:44,560
the colony had waited without rescue.

20
00:00:45,220 --> 00:00:46,600
By the time he returned,

21
00:00:47,460 --> 00:00:49,820
years had passed and the settlers had

22
00:00:49,830 --> 00:00:52,074
been left to survive without help.

23
00:00:52,874 --> 00:00:55,160
Maybe the settlers moved inland.

24
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:57,980
Maybe they joined Indigenous communities.

25
00:00:58,840 --> 00:01:00,520
Maybe hunger, disease,

26
00:01:00,840 --> 00:01:02,960
or violence ended their journey.

27
00:01:03,680 --> 00:01:05,880
No one left a record explaining what

28
00:01:05,890 --> 00:01:06,973
happened to them all.

29
00:01:08,080 --> 00:01:10,400
The English remembered it as the Lost

30
00:01:10,410 --> 00:01:13,240
Colony. But this was not an empty

31
00:01:13,250 --> 00:01:16,120
wilderness waiting for a European mystery.

32
00:01:16,130 --> 00:01:19,700
Indigenous communities already lived here,

33
00:01:19,800 --> 00:01:21,360
and they may have seen the settlers'

34
00:01:21,370 --> 00:01:26,100
fear, flight, or disappearance from a side

35
00:01:26,110 --> 00:01:28,180
the surviving records never preserved.

36
00:01:29,700 --> 00:01:32,180
Roanoke still offers no final answer.

37
00:01:32,840 --> 00:01:35,440
The surviving records cannot tell us who

38
00:01:35,450 --> 00:01:37,020
lived, who died,

39
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:38,940
or where the settlers went.

40
00:01:38,950 --> 00:01:42,080
What remains is the terror of isolation,

41
00:01:42,090 --> 00:01:45,300
and the knowledge that an entire community

42
00:01:45,310 --> 00:01:48,420
can vanish without leaving a clear explanation.
